## Before Working

1. Read `docs/PLAYBOOK.md` — session entry point, identifies active lifecycle phase
2. If in execution phase: Read `docs/CURRENT_WORK.md` → `context/WORKING.md` → Phase SPEC.md
3. Sync: `git fetch origin && git log --oneline HEAD..origin/$(git branch --show-current) | head -5`

## Development Loop (Non-Negotiable)

**No code without scenarios. No scenarios without acceptance criteria.** One loop for every runtime; the same
stages as the framework's `DEV_LOOP.md` §1, in this order:

| # | Stage | Exit condition |
|-|-|-|
| 0 | draft red-team | premise checklist recorded on the design artifact (diagnosis grounded; cheaper alternative considered; consumers read); a full independent pass only when the artifact changes policy or gates, is consumed by more than one seat or runtime, or is irreversible or migration-bearing |
| 1 | scope | SPEC.md + SCENARIOS.md exist; every named API, number or consumer claim is cited or refused |
| 2 | spec-audit | independent fresh-context audit; every blocker dispositioned |
| 3 | RED | scenarios run and FAIL: runner exit non-zero, recorded (Quick scope may satisfy RED as the same change) |
| 4 | GREEN | implementation; the same runner exits zero; `{{ type_check_command }}` passes |
| 5 | review | no unresolved actionable finding; the complete gate in `.claude/skills/orchestrators/verify/complete.md` passes (scenario evidence RED then GREEN, SPEC adherence line by line, audits and best-practice checks, `{{ type_check_command }}`, build); hard block on missing scenarios |
| 6 | integrate | checks green on the current head; only the integrator merges |
| 7 | document | doc delta, or an explicit `no-doc-impact: <reason>` line in the PR body; fails like a test gate |
| 8 | capture | every discovery has a durable record (issue, hub or `context/DISCOVERIES.md`); nothing lives only in a session |

The gate definitions are the same files for every runtime; Claude Code runs them as commands (map in `CLAUDE.md`),
other runtimes read the files and perform each section.

**Scope classification:**

| Trigger (ANY match) | Scope | TDD Required? |
|-|-|-|
| New DB tables/columns | Standard+ | Yes |
| New API routes | Standard+ | Yes |
| New UI pages/major components | Standard+ | Yes |
| 4+ files modified | Standard+ | Yes |
| Single-file bug fix, no new surface area | Quick | No |

## Work Routing

| Source | Route |
|-|-|
| Quick fix (single-file, no new surface area) | Fix → Commit with `Fixes #N` → document (or `no-doc-impact`) → capture |
| Standard+ (see scope triggers) | stages 0–8: scope → spec-audit → RED → GREEN → review → integrate → document → capture |
| External concern | Append to `context/DISCOVERIES.md` (stage 8) → keep working |

For dispatch/handoff summaries and scoped evidence comparison, use `docs/DELIVERY.md`.
It consolidates the work reference; existing entry, review and effect gates still apply.

## Skills

Canonical skills live in `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (Codex reads them there); `.claude/skills/<name>/` is
the byte-identical generated projection for Claude Code — never edit the projection by hand. Before implementing
20+ lines, invoke the matching best-practices skill; if a skill's information is wrong or outdated, update the skill
immediately.

Before using `ponytail` or `caveman`, read `docs/SKILL_MODES.md` and apply the mode it sets for your
responsibility. Upstream defaults do not apply: `caveman` runs `lite` for routine updates and never compresses
exact facts, code, errors, numbers, ordering, requested detail, warnings, handoffs, verdicts or records; `ponytail`
narrows implementations, never requirements, evidence or gates.

## Development Protocol

For each PROGRESS.md item: implement → check off → commit. If exit landmarks met → Signal `[PHASE_COMPLETE]`.

